        "key": "pc_minimum_guarantee_uprating",
        "parameters": [
          "gov.dwp.pension_credit.guarantee_credit.minimum_guarantee.SINGLE"
        ],
        "reason": "The installed model raises the Pension Credit standard minimum guarantee by lagged calendar-year CPI, 2.3% in April 2027, but the law requires at least the growth in earnings, 3.9% in May to July 2026 (Social Security Administration Act 1992 s. 150A(2)). So the guarantee is too low from 2027, and so are the pension-age Housing Benefit allowances and the savings credit threshold, which the same fix covers; a change to the earnings input misses them. policyengine-uk #2557, the fix for #2533, keeps the guarantee on lagged CPI. Until a fix that uprates it by earnings is in the model, measures touching these from 2027 are held at provisional."
      }
